1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,660
I'd been driving for
almost 11 hours when the

2
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,500
detour signs pushed me off the interstate.

3
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:20,000
The road narrowed to two
lanes, then the radio

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,340
lost its station, and for a long time the

5
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:24,140
only light out there
was my own headlights.

6
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:28,860
Around two in the morning, I saw a gas
station sign glowing over the fields.

7
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:34,060
The pumps were on, the store was dark, and
there was one other car parked by the air

8
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,860
machine with its engine
running and nobody inside.

9
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:40,160
This was in October, about six years ago.

10
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:45,020
I was 24 and moving back home to Missouri
after a job in Colorado fell apart.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,380
Everything I owned was in the backseat
of a Corolla with a cracked windshield.

12
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:52,220
I'd planned to stop for the
night in a motel somewhere

13
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,700
in western Kansas, but I kept telling

14
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,820
myself one more hour, and
by the time the detour

15
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,720
came up, I was too tired to be smart

16
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,500
about it.

17
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,340
I pulled up to the pump,
farthest from the other car.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,940
It was an older station wagon, dark green
with wood panels on the sides and a bumper

19
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,100
sticker that said, Proud
Parent of an Honor Student,

20
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,500
with the name of the school scratched

21
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,300
off.

22
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,300
The exhaust was rising in the cold.

23
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,700
The headlights were off,
but the dome light was

24
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,800
on, and I could see a
jacket on the passenger

25
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,760
seat and a fast food bag on the dashboard.

26
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,780
I figured whoever it
belonged to was in the

27
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:24,700
bathroom around the side of the building.

28
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:27,000
I filled the tank and waited.

29
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,340
I don't know why I waited.

30
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,680
I think I wanted to see someone walk back
to that car, just so I could stop thinking

31
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,480
about it.

32
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,940
Nobody came.

33
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,440
The pump clicked off,
the screen asked if I

34
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,760
wanted a receipt, and the whole time that

35
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:43,360
engine kept idling, steady, like
it had been running for hours.

36
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,720
I didn't go check the bathroom.

37
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,700
I got back in my car and left.

38
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,420
About twenty minutes later, the
detour signs ended at a truck stop.

39
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:55,640
It was the first real building
I'd seen in a long time.

40
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,760
A diner on one side, a
couple of semis parked

41
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,940
out back with their running lights on, and

42
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:04,700
a sign that said, Open 24 hours,
with two of the letters burned out.

43
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,660
I parked near the
entrance because I needed

44
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,880
coffee, and I needed to sit somewhere with

45
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,740
people for a while.

46
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:15,620
Inside, it was warm and smelled
like burnt coffee and bacon grease.

47
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:18,020
There was a trucker at
the counter, reading

48
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,460
his phone, an older man asleep in a booth

49
00:02:20,460 --> 00:02:21,880
by the window, and one waitress.

50
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,480
Her name tag said D.
She looked about fifty,

51
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,740
and she called me Honey
before I'd even sat

52
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:28,540
down.

53
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,680
I took a booth facing
the door, ordered coffee

54
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,700
and a slice of pie, and started looking at

55
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:38,040
the map on my phone, trying to figure
out how far I was from anything.

56
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,460
That's when the couple came in.

57
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,000
They were young, maybe my age.

58
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,960
The guy wore a gray
hoodie, and the girl had

59
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,120
on a denim jacket that
was too thin for the

60
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:49,920
weather.

61
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,140
It had started to rain
outside, and the shoulders

62
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:53,560
of their jackets were dark with it.

63
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,520
They were arguing in that low,
tight way people argue in public.

64
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,200
As they walked past my
booth, the girl said,

65
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,620
Every single time, Ray.

66
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:02,960
Every single time.

67
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,560
He didn't answer.

68
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,580
They sat two booths down
from me, across the

69
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,980
aisle, and D. went over with menus and two

70
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,060
waters like it was nothing.

71
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,480
I didn't think much about it.

72
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:14,960
I ate my pie.

73
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:17,900
I heard bits of their
conversation, something about

74
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,260
a wrong turn and whose idea it had been

75
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,140
to leave so late.

76
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:24,480
The girl had a laugh that
wasn't really a laugh.

77
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,900
At one point, Ray said, We'll be fine.

78
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,100
We're almost there.

79
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:29,740
She didn't say anything back.

80
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:32,640
After a while, I got up
to use the restroom.

81
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:35,220
It was at the end of a short
hallway past the kitchen.

82
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,520
I remember the hallway
because one of the fluorescent

83
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,020
lights was flickering, and there

84
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:42,340
was a corkboard on the wall with business
cards and a flyer for a missing dog.

85
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:45,060
I was in there maybe
three or four minutes.

86
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,900
I washed my hands,
splashed water on my face,

87
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:50,080
and looked at myself in
the mirror, thinking

88
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,620
I really needed to find a bed.

89
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:56,880
When I came out and walked back toward my
booth, the bell over the front door rang.

90
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,580
It was them, the same
couple, gray hoodie, thin

91
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:03,940
denim jacket, the
shoulders of both jackets

92
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:04,740
dark with rain.

93
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,680
They walked in the same
way, him a step ahead,

94
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,720
her a little behind with her arms crossed,

95
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:15,520
and as they passed me, the girl said,
Every single time, Ray, every single time.

96
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,500
I stopped in the aisle.

97
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,740
I looked over at the booth two down
from mine, where they'd been sitting.

98
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,040
It was empty.

99
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:25,760
No menus, no glasses, no
wet rings on the table.

100
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,660
It had been wiped down like
nobody had used it all night.

101
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,100
They sat in that same booth.

102
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,440
Dee came over with two
menus and two waters, and

103
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,900
she smiled at them, and she said, Evening

104
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,700
you two.

105
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:38,620
Rough night out there?

106
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,300
Exactly how you'd greet
someone who just walked in.

107
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:45,000
I sat down because I didn't
know what else to do.

108
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:46,740
My coffee was still there.

109
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,760
My plate was still there.

110
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,340
I watched them.

111
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,020
I kept waiting for one
of them to look at me,

112
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,260
or laugh, or for this to turn into some

113
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,060
kind of joke.

114
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:56,980
Ray was rubbing his eyes.

115
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:59,680
The girl was looking out the
window at the parking lot.

116
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,480
They were having the same conversation.

117
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,060
Wrong turn.

118
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:05,180
Leaving too late.

119
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,080
And then Ray said, We'll be fine.

120
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,100
We're almost there.

121
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,320
I looked at the trucker at the counter.

122
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:12,880
He hadn't looked up from
his phone the whole time.

123
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,740
The old man in the window
booth was still asleep.

124
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:19,140
Nobody else in that room seemed
to think anything was wrong.

125
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:22,200
I left a twenty on the
table and walked out.

126
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,480
I didn't wait for change.

127
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:27,300
When I got outside, the rain had
stopped, and the parking lot was dry.

128
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:28,500
Completely dry.

129
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:29,880
No puddles.

130
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,120
Nothing wet on my windshield.

131
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,440
I stood there for a second,
looking at the ground.

132
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,240
Then I got in my car,
locked the doors, and sat

133
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:39,140
with the engine running for a long time.

134
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,000
I didn't want to drive past
that gas station again.

135
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,280
I didn't want to go back inside, either.

136
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,260
So I just sat there
until the sky started to

137
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,260
turn gray, and then I followed the signs

138
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,060
back to the interstate.

139
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,400
I didn't pass the gas
station on the way back.

140
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:56,140
I took the same road.

141
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:56,980
I'm sure of that.

142
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,500
It just wasn't there.

143
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:02,340
I had a dash cam back then,
one of those cheap ones

144
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:04,160
that records over itself every few hours.

145
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,560
When I finally got home
and checked it, most

146
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,860
of that night had
already been overwritten.

147
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,440
The only file left starts
as I pull into the truck

148
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,420
stop parking lot at 2.14 in the morning.

149
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:18,000
I park, the camera keeps
recording, and about

150
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,220
a minute later, the dark
green station wagon

151
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:22,160
pulls into the spot right in front of me.

152
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:25,500
Engine running, dome
light on, nobody inside.

153
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,220
The date on that clip is October 14th.

154
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:32,100
The year is the one before
I ever drove that road.

155
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:35,620
I still drive that interstate
a couple of times a year.

156
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,660
If the detour signs are
up, I don't take them.

157
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:41,700
I find the last town
before the exit, I park

158
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,960
somewhere well lit, and I sleep in my car

159
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:44,760
until morning.

